Misparented table-internal boxes had no fixup at all, in either
direction:

- display:table-cell/-row/-row-group children of a non-table parent
  fell through construct's Flow branch and stacked vertically as
  independent blocks. Legacy pages using table-cell for columns or
  vertical centering rendered as a single column.
- Non-table content inside a display:table container was dropped
  outright by collect_table_cells ('probably a caption: ignore'):
  display:table centering wrappers lost their content entirely.

Fixes:
- construct: runs of table-internal children collect into an
  anonymous display:table wrapper (LayoutChildren grows an
  anonymous_table_id mirroring the anonymous-block machinery; the
  wrapper's display comes from a new ::-servo-anonymous-table UA
  rule). Whitespace between table-internal boxes is dropped instead
  of terminating the run. The Flow fast paths defer to the complex
  collector whenever a table-internal child is present.
- table: cells outside any real row open an implicit row (consecutive
  strays share it; a real row or group closes it), and non-table
  children inside a table become anonymous cells in their own
  implicit row instead of vanishing.

WPT CSS2/tables: table-anonymous-objects-012 style stray-cell tests
drop from ~5% pixel-diff to near-miss; content-in-table no longer
disappears. The remaining anonymous-objects deltas are table sizing
parity (column distribution for mixed stray/real structures), a
separate project.

Implicit rows push an anonymous TableRow (null node id, so no row
background paints) and place cells through ColumnCursor. The
incremental anonymous-box restyle re-cascades anonymous tables with
::-servo-anonymous-table instead of the anonymous-box style.
